---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import graph from '../data/researchGraph.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const internal = (segment) => `${base}/${segment.replace(/^\//, '')}`;
const nodeById = new Map(graph.nodes.map((node) => [node.id, node]));
const chain = graph.canonical_chain.map((id) => nodeById.get(id)).filter(Boolean);
const researchObjects = graph.nodes.filter((node) => ['paper', 'draft', 'institutional_proposal'].includes(node.type));
---
<Layout title="Provenance" description="Standards-first research provenance for Agalmic Research using W3C PROV, RO-Crate and CRediT with a narrow experimental epistemic and possibility-portfolio extension layer.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Research provenance</p>
      <h1>Preserve the path without inventing another provenance island.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Agalmic Research originally built a local discovery graph before adequately surveying mature provenance standards. That graph remains as historical evidence. New work uses W3C PROV concepts, RO-Crate packaging and CRediT wherever they already solve the problem.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Correction</p>
        <h2>The local graph is an experiment, not a new standard.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">Provenance, contributorship and graph-based scholarly communication already have substantial prior art.</p>
        <p><a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-dm/">W3C PROV</a> models entities, activities, agents, attribution, derivation and responsibility. <a href="https://www.researchobject.org/ro-crate/specification/1.3/">RO-Crate</a> packages research objects in machine-readable JSON-LD. <a href="https://credit.niso.org/">CRediT</a> standardizes scholarly contribution roles. <a href="https://www.mira.science/">MIRA</a> demonstrates graph-based questions, claims and evidence with granular attribution.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Use established provenance vocabulary wherever it fits. Extend only where the research problem genuinely requires information it cannot express.</strong></p></div>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch/blob/main/docs/STANDARDS_PROVENANCE_PROFILE.md">Read the standards-first provenance profile ↗</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Standards stack</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>Reuse first. Extend second.</h2>
          <p>The layers answer different questions and should not be collapsed into a single project-specific schema.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="status-grid">
        <div><strong>W3C PROV</strong><span>Who or what generated, used, influenced, derived or was associated with a research entity or activity?</span></div>
        <div><strong>CRediT</strong><span>Which standardized scholarly contribution roles did a human contributor perform?</span></div>
        <div><strong>RO-Crate</strong><span>How is the research object, its files and contextual metadata packaged for exchange and preservation?</span></div>
        <div><strong>Agalmic extension</strong><span>What is the claim-level authority state, branch state, handoff need, search boundary, reversal condition or possibility-portfolio status?</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="muted">W3C PROV's term <code>SoftwareAgent</code> is a provenance category. Using it for an AI system does not imply that the system is a moral person, legal author, epistemic knower or scientific discoverer.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Machine-readable artefacts</p>
        <h2>The migration is now being exercised session by session.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The repository contains an experimental <strong>RO-Crate 1.3 metadata document</strong>, a <strong>PROV-O-aligned JSON-LD projection</strong> for the earlier lineage review, and a separate PROV-O-aligned session bundle for the possibility-portfolio / Active Frontier work.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch/blob/main/ro-crate-metadata.json">RO-Crate metadata ↗</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch/blob/main/src/data/provenance/2026-09-07-frontier-system.jsonld">Frontier-session provenance ↗</a>
        </div>
        <p class="muted">“PROV-O-aligned JSON-LD” means the documents use PROV ontology terms in JSON-LD. It does not claim conformance to every serialization profile or certification by W3C.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell thesis">
      <p class="eyebrow">Chain currently under scrutiny</p>
      <blockquote>Cognitive abundance → authorial capacity gap → defensible stewardship → separable contribution and authority → epistemic handoff → epistemic uptake scarcity → institutions for routing knowledge.</blockquote>
      <p>The novelty review found antecedents for every major link. The chain is retained as a synthesis and research genealogy, not as evidence that Agalmic Research discovered seven new principles.</p>
      <p><a href={internal('lineage')}>Inspect the intellectual lineage →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Possibility layer</p>
        <h2>Provenance should preserve branches without turning them into obligations.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">The Memory Palace records the topology of the search. The Possibility Portfolio records what deserves another move.</p>
        <p>Public-safe possibilities now have explicit states such as seed, option, active, handoff, realized, parked and retired. The state is an operating decision, not an epistemic truth. A parked or retired branch keeps its provenance, rationale and potential reversal condition.</p>
        <p><a href={internal('frontier')}>Inspect the public possibility portfolio →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Two records</p>
        <h2>Contribution provenance is not epistemic authority.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">Standards can tell us a great deal about contribution and derivation without proving a claim true.</p>
        <p>CRediT and PROV should record contribution and process. A separate experimental authority layer records which claims, if any, a person or institution can presently defend and the evidence supporting that status.</p>
        <div class="status-grid">
          <div><strong>Contribution</strong><span>Use CRediT for human scholarly roles where it fits and preserve finer process descriptors only when materially useful.</span></div>
          <div><strong>Authority</strong><span>Record claim-sensitive support such as expert review, empirical evidence, formal verification, reproduction or demonstrated defence. Do not infer it from contribution.</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Origin deserves credit. Authority requires warrant.</strong></p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Session protocol</p>
        <h2>Capture discovery while it is happening.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">The Memory Palace Protocol records the shape of a research search, not hidden model reasoning.</p>
        <p>It preserves visible prompts and outputs, sources, artefacts, decisions, branch states, roads not taken, search boundaries, contribution roles and authority changes. The companion Possibility Portfolio prompt captures materially new ideas as options and constrains the Active Frontier.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href={internal('memory-palace-protocol')}>Read the combined protocol page</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={internal('frontier')}>Active Frontier</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Historical local graph</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>Do not rewrite the first map after learning cartography.</h2>
          <p>The v0.1 local graph predates the standards-first correction. It is preserved because that history is itself provenance. Future projections can map it into PROV rather than pretending the project began with the later design.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index-list">
        {chain.map((node, i) => (
          <article class="index-item">
            <span class="index-meta">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{node.label}</h3>
              <p class="muted">{node.summary}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="index-status">{node.epistemic_status}</span>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button secondary" href={internal('research-graph.json')}>View historical graph JSON</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Human + machine process</p>
        <h2>Record events without prematurely settling agency.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Distributed-discovery scholarship makes a flat “human author + AI assistance” statement insufficient. A session may distribute problem framing, candidate generation, significance recognition, validation, integration and realization across different actors.</p>
        <p><strong>Human curator:</strong> has initiated core questions, directed search, selected or rejected branches, recognized promising connections and made publication decisions.</p>
        <p><strong>OpenAI ChatGPT:</strong> has materially contributed literature search, candidate generation, terminology, synthesis, criticism, drafting and repository transformations.</p>
        <p>PROV can record those activities and associations. It should not be used to smuggle in the philosophical conclusion that either participant alone “discovered” the resulting knowledge.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Research objects</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>Papers and proposals retain their genealogy.</h2>
          <p>The local graph still records early contribution reconstruction. New research objects additionally carry standards-oriented provenance, lineage status and, where relevant, possibility-portfolio state.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index-list">
        {researchObjects.map((node, i) => (
          <article class="index-item">
            <span class="index-meta">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{node.label}</h3>
              <p class="muted">{node.summary}</p>
              {node.repository_path && <p><code>{node.repository_path}</code></p>}
            </div>
            <span class="index-status">{node.epistemic_status}</span>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Memory-palace direction</p>
        <h2>Eventually, navigate both discovery and choice.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">The long-term interface remains a navigable research memory palace.</p>
        <p>A reader should be able to enter at a claim and travel backward through sources and activities, sideways into competing branches and objections, and forward into validation, handoff, implementation and correction. A researcher should also be able to see which branches are active, preserved as options, parked or retired, without confusing portfolio status with truth.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>